## Summary

Profiles must be members-only. This pins the boundary with feature
tests: logged-out visitors are sent to login before any profile surface,
and no member data appears in any public page or its source.

## Changes

- Add tests/Feature/Profile/MemberDirectoryExposureTest.php (6 tests):
  - logged-out GET /profile and /members/{id} redirect to login
  - logged-out PATCH /members/{id} redirects to login, writes nothing
- member-adjacent JSON (/events.json, /events/{event}, RSVP PUT/DELETE)
redirects to login
- Livewire MemberProfile mount 403s guests (livewire/update bypasses
route middleware)
- public pages (/, /events, /events/past, /join, sitemap, /e/{event},
RSS, per-event ICS, whole-calendar feed) carry no member strings
- RSVP aggregate count stays public ("1 going") while names stay inside

## Testing

- tests/Feature/Profile/MemberDirectoryExposureTest.php: 6 passed (64
assertions)
- tests/Feature/Profile/ full directory: 43 passed (285 assertions)
- neighbors (Profile + DiscordLoginTest + Sitemap + RobotsTxt): 75
passed (455 assertions)

Refs: TOG-5621

