Subject: [PATCH 03/48] feat(events): show spots-left capacity signal on event
 page (#383)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary
Event pages now show an explicit capacity progress signal next to the
going count: `X of Y spots left` when seats remain, `Full` when none do,
and nothing when the event has no cap. Reads the existing
`capacity`/`going_count` data — no schema change, no new query.

## Changes
- `resources/views/events/show.blade.php`: `event-spots-left` badge
beside the going count; `Full` when spots reach zero (clamped, so
over-subscribed caps never print a negative); nothing rendered for
uncapped events.
- `tests/Feature/Events/EventPageTest.php`: four tests — available,
full, over-capacity-clamped, and unknown states.

## Testing
- `php -l` on both files: clean.
- `pint --test` on the test file: passed.
- `php artisan view:cache` + `view:clear`: Blade compiles.
- Full Pest suite needs Postgres (not available in this container per
`phpunit.xml`); CI `pest` job is the verification gate for the four new
tests.

Refs: TOG-6924

