 single writer (#467)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

Per the [TOG-8433](/TOG/issues/TOG-8433) decision spec
([TOG-6965](/TOG/issues/TOG-6965) found HTTP PATCH and Livewire
enforcing different games-limit rules): Livewire is canonical, the HTTP
PATCH writer is deleted. `MemberProfile::save()` is now the single
profile writer.

## Changes

- Removed `PATCH /members/{user}` (`profiles.update`) from
`routes/web.php`.
- Removed `ProfileController@update` (kept `mine`/`show`).
- Deleted `UpdateProfileRequest` and `profileAttributes()` (no other
callers).
- Hoisted shared Livewire rules into `MemberProfile::validationRules()`
(used by `save()`, pinned by the upload-surface tripwire).
- Ported unique HTTP-path coverage into
`tests/Feature/Livewire/MemberProfileTest.php` (21-lines-with-dups saves
20; >20 distinct rejected; 80-char name limit; bio/timezone/control-char
rules; non-owner save blocked; PATCH now 405s; `profiles.update` name
gone).
- `ProfileBackendTest` keeps GET read-path pins; access-log, production
route allowlist, upload-surface tripwire and policy comments follow the
deletion; docs updated.

## Testing

- `php -l` clean on all touched files.
- Full Pest suite not runnable on this box (no Postgres, PHP 8.3 vs
required 8.4) — relying on CI (pr-lint + test suite) for verification.
- Acceptance greps: `profileAttributes` zero hits in app/; `gamesText`
writer only in `app/Livewire/MemberProfile.php`.

Refs: TOG-8440

