Subject: [PATCH 14/48] ci(deps): gate lockfiles on composer and npm audit
 (#473)

## Summary

CI pins actions to SHAs but never audits dependencies. This adds a
`deps-audit` job failing on high/critical advisories from
`composer.lock` and `package-lock.json`, wired into the `tests`
aggregate, with fail-closed predicates in `ci/deps-audit.sh` and an
offline selftest in `static`.

## Changes

- New `deps-audit` CI job: `composer audit` + `npm audit`, no
install/vendor/node_modules/database, free public feeds only
- New `ci/deps-audit.sh`: JSON predicates (allowlist low/medium, fail on
high/critical/unknown/malformed), `--selftest` on canned fixtures
- Pin wiring: `static` runs the selftest, `verify-pipeline.sh` check 13,
audit live case, seven-check protection lists, `docs/ci.md`

## Testing

- `./ci/deps-audit.sh --selftest` on head `6e9448a`: 10/10 PASS
(verified this run)
- Prior run: gate exits 0 on today's lockfiles, 1 naming `minimist
[critical]` on the breakage fixture
- CI must go red/green on this PR per acceptance (pending run)

## Checklist

- [x] No secrets, real `.env`, `vendor/` or `node_modules/` in the diff
- [x] No changes to `app/Http/Resources/EventResource.php`
- [ ] `composer check` green on the PR (pending CI run)

