From f2ff4137bfa79e5e804097a556c07bd9cbe1a2d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "togetherweown[bot]"
 <319968614+togetherweown[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:14:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/48] feat(ics): add ETag conditional-GET to collection and
 per-event downloads (#475)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

Calendar clients polling `GET /events.ics` and `GET
/events/{event_key}.ics` re-download the full body on every poll —
neither surface sent a validator. This adds strong-ETag-over-bytes +
`If-None-Match` -> 304 to both, mirroring the RSS/JSON pattern
(TOG-7330).

The trap: `EventIcs::vevent()` stamped `DTSTAMP` with `now('UTC')`, so
no two renders shared bytes and a naive byte-hash ETag would never
match. `DTSTAMP` now rides the content clock (the row's `updated_at`,
RFC 5545-correct — the entry's last-revision instant), so unchanged
content renders byte-identical bodies. Empty collection stays
byte-stable (no VEVENT lines to stamp).

## Changes

- `EventFeedController`, `EventIcsController`: `setEtag(sha256(bytes))`
+ `isNotModified($request)`, same shape as `EventRssController`.
- `EventIcs::dtstamp()`: content-clock stamp; `?? 0` fallback
unreachable from both controllers (persisted rows only).
- `EventEtagTest`: 7 new tests — 304 + no body on repeat poll (both
routes, incl. empty collection), byte-stable re-renders, new ETag after
in-scope edit.

## Testing

- `php artisan test tests/Feature/Events/EventEtagTest.php` — 13 passed
(52 assertions)
- `php artisan test tests/Feature/Events` — 228 passed (967 assertions)
- `./vendor/bin/pint --test` on the 4 touched files — passed
- Slice cherry-picked from batch branch; 4 files byte-identical to
Code-Reviewer-APPROVED `fd1fc43` ([TOG-9285](/TOG/issues/TOG-9285));
shared batch branch untouched.

