From: "togetherweown[bot]"
 <319968614+togetherweown[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:35:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/48] fix(events): settle terminal Discord refusals instead
 of re-dispatching forever (#477)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

A terminal bot refusal (`retryable: false`, e.g. `action_not_allowed`)
made `SyncEventToDiscord` call `fail()` — but left the row shaped
exactly like a transient outage (published, `discord_event_id` null).
The reconcile pass matches that shape, so it re-dispatched the refused
operation every ten minutes forever: a `failed_jobs` row and spent bot
budget per pass, for an answer already given, while the member read
"Syncing…" indefinitely.

This PR stamps terminally-refused rows (`discord_sync_failed_at` + code)
so reconcile skips them, re-arms the stamp on a genuinely new
member/moderator change, and gives the banner its third state (saved
here, refused over there) instead of "Syncing…" forever.

## Changes

- `SyncEventToDiscord`: all terminal paths (`retryable: false` refusal,
`not_configured`, dead agent grant) stamp
`discord_sync_failed_at`/`discord_sync_failure_code` via
`markTerminallyRefused()`; success clears the stamp.
- `ReconcileEvents::resyncStaleEvents()`: skips stamped rows
(`whereNull('discord_sync_failed_at')`).
- `EventService::syncAfterCommit()`: clears the stamp on a genuinely new
change (outside the unique-lock savepoint, so a failed clear is never a
silent skip).
- `RsvpButton` + blade: third banner state `rsvp-sync-failed` ("Saved.
Discord sync didn't go through — your spot is still held."),
`role=status`; component refreshes its event after a re-arming write so
the banner doesn't go stale.
- `Event` model: new fillable/casts, excluded from activity log (bot
bookkeeping).
- Migration `2026_09_28_000100` adds the two stamp columns.
- New `TerminalSyncRefusalTest` (5 tests): stamp set, reconcile skips,
re-arm clears + re-dispatches, banner third state, dead-grant stamp +
skip.

## Testing

- `TerminalSyncRefusalTest`: 5 pass, 22 assertions (Postgres
`two_web_test` via `paperclip-db`).
- Regressions: `SyncEventToDiscordTest` + `ReconcileEventsCommandTest` +
`RsvpWriteBackFailureTest` + `EventLifecycleTest` (48 pass, 152
assertions); `RsvpButtonTest` + `EventEtagTest` +
`EventJsonContractTest` + `AuditTrailTest` + `RsvpUniqueLockRaceTest`
(56 pass, 209 assertions).
- `vendor/bin/pint` clean; `vendor/bin/phpstan` no errors on all touched
files.
- Note: this worktree has no `APP_KEY`/`.env`, so Livewire tests need a
throwaway `APP_KEY` env for the run; pre-existing gap, unrelated to this
change (existing `RsvpButtonTest` fails identically without it).

