Subject: [PATCH 22/48] feat(profile): name the expired session on save/cancel
 with a way back in (#481)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

A member composing a long profile edit past the 120-minute
SESSION_LIFETIME lost the submit to the silent expired-session path
(TOG-8137). Save/cancel arriving with no signed-in member now sets
`sessionExpired` and renders a `role=alert` banner with a login link,
keeping the member's input intact. Mirrors the RSVP session-expired path
(TOG-8135).

## Changes

- `app/Livewire/MemberProfile.php`: `sessionExpired` flag; explicit
signed-out check before the gate in `save()`/`cancel()`; cleared on
`edit()` and authenticated save.
- `resources/views/livewire/member-profile.blade.php`: expired-session
banner (`data-testid=profile-session-expired`); focus listener
prioritises it.
- `tests/Feature/Livewire/MemberProfileTest.php`: 5 new tests
(save-signed-out, cancel-signed-out, alert semantics, cleared on auth
save, cleared on reopen).

## Testing

- `php artisan test tests/Feature/Livewire/MemberProfileTest.php
tests/Feature/Livewire/RsvpButtonTest.php` — 78 passed, 336 assertions.
- Pint clean.

Refs: TOG-8137

