Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/48] fix(profile): serialise first save behind parent row
 lock (#483)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

Two concurrent first-time profile saves both missed the `updateOrCreate`
SELECT and both INSERTed; the loser died on `profiles_user_id_unique`
(SQLSTATE 23505, raw 500). The single writer (`MemberProfile::save()`,
the only writer since TOG-8440 deleted the PATCH path) now goes through
a small `SaveMemberProfile` action that takes `lockForUpdate()` on the
parent `users` row inside a transaction — the same serialisation shape
`EventService` uses. The loser waits for the winner's commit, sees the
row, and its write becomes an UPDATE.

## Changes

- `app/Support/Profiles/SaveMemberProfile.php` (new): transactional
writer, parent row lock first, then the existing `updateOrCreate`.
- `app/Livewire/MemberProfile.php`: `save()` calls the new action (test
seam `$profileWriter` untouched).
- `tests/Integration/ProfileCreationRaceTest.php` +
`tests/Support/profile_race_worker.php` (new): two OS processes gated on
the held parent lock; asserts the lock-queue shape (row=1, total=2) plus
exactly one profile row, and an update-path pin.

## Testing

- `pest --testsuite=Integration`: 7 passed (26 assertions), incl. 3x
repeat of the race test.
- Profile feature files (Livewire MemberProfileTest +
ProfileBackendTest): 40 passed.
- `pint --test` passed; `phpstan` no errors on changed app files.
- Negative control: same gate against the old bare `updateOrCreate`
yields row=0/total=2, so the test fails on the old mechanism.

Refs: TOG-6966

