 <319968614+togetherweown[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:20:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/48] security(agent-events): throttle POST /api/agent-events
 per credential (#459)

## Summary

Adds an outer route shield (`throttle:agent-events`, 60/min per
credential with IP fallback for anonymous hits) in front of the
per-grant service budgets, closing the unthrottled machine ingress while
human join callbacks already carry `throttle:10,1`.

## Changes

- `routes/api.php`: `POST /api/agent-events` carries
`throttle:agent-events`
- `app/Support/AgentEventRateLimit.php`: new `routeLimit()` keyed by
SHA-256 of the bearer credential (never the credential, never per-IP for
admitted callers behind shared egress)
- `app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`: registers the named limiter
(route-cache safe)
- `config/agent-events.php`: `route_per_minute` (default 60, above the
10+30 inner budgets so the bot burst never sees it)
- `tests/Feature/AgentEvents/AgentEventIngressTest.php`: 4 new tests
(route pin, burst-under-shield + 429 envelope, per-credential buckets,
unauthenticated flood refused before DB)

Both layers throw `ThrottleRequestsException`, so the TOG-6788 429
envelope is one shape whichever fires.

## Testing

- `php -l` clean on all 5 files
- `route:list` shows `ThrottleRequests:agent-events` on the route;
`route:cache` + clear round-trip OK
- Limiter unit-checked via tinker (credential hash key, 60/min, IP
fallback)
- `pint --test` passed on all 5 files
- Full Pest suite NOT run locally (no Postgres in this workspace);
relies on CI

Refs: TOG-8402

