Subject: [PATCH 33/48] feat(events): show skeleton while member-started
 re-renders load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary
Adds a loading state to /events. Before this change, the page showed
nothing while a member-started Livewire round trip (view toggle, month
steps, the past drawer, clearing a search) was in flight. The RSVP
"Can't make it" button also froze silently while its request ran.
TOG-5318's empty-state work adds no loading markup, so this PR covers
only that gap. It is preview-safe and changes no backend behaviour.

## Changes
- `events-calendar.blade.php`: one `role="status"` skeleton (3 pulse
cards, screen-reader text "Loading events…"). It is hidden up front with
an inline `display:none` (TOG-6351 pattern) and shown with
`wire:loading.flex` for `setView, previousMonth, nextMonth, showPast,
clearSearch, retryLoad`. The live content is wrapped in
`wire:loading.remove` on the same targets, so the skeleton and the
content never render together. Debounced search typing is deliberately
not a target.
- The action buttons get `wire:loading.attr="disabled"` scoped to their
own action.
- `rsvp-button.blade.php`: the withdraw button gets the same spinner,
wait copy and aria-busy contract as "I'm in".
- `EventsCalendar.php`: the docblock no longer says the component has no
loading state.
- `retryLoad` is targeted ahead of TOG-5318; an unknown target is inert
until that method lands.

## Testing
- `php -l app/Livewire/EventsCalendar.php`: no syntax errors.
- Added 5 Pest cases to `EventsCalendarTest` and 1 to `RsvpButtonTest`.
They could not run locally: the worker has no Postgres (`SQLSTATE[08006]
connection refused` on 127.0.0.1:5432). CI is the verification.
- Not yet checked in a browser on staging.

Refs: TOG-5416

