Subject: [PATCH 38/48] security(csp): report-only mode plus violation sink
 (#491)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

CSP was enforced but violations were invisible: no report-only mode, no
report endpoint. This adds a `CSP_REPORT_ONLY` toggle plus a
session-free `POST /csp-reports` sink that logs and samples.

## Changes

- `AddContentSecurityPolicy`: with `csp.report_only` on, emits
`Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` (same policy plus `report-uri
/csp-reports`); enforcement output byte-identical with the flag off.
- New `CspReportController`: accepts both browser report shapes, logs a
sampled fixed key set (never the raw body), always 204, 8 KB cap; empty
funnel middleware stack, no throttle (cache is the DB everywhere
shipped).
- New `config/csp.php`; `CSP_REPORT_ONLY` / `CSP_REPORT_SAMPLE_RATE` in
`.env.example`.
- `tests/Unit/ProductionRouteAllowlistTest.php`: allowlists `POST
csp-reports`, drops the two stale design-lab lines left by the TOG-5632
merge (pre-existing red on main, proven via stash; the test header names
the merger for exactly this).

## Testing

- `pest tests/Feature/CspReportOnlyTest.php` (new, 10 tests):
report-only header swap, enforcement parity, both report shapes logged,
always-204 on malformed, oversize cap, no-raw-body, no-middleware,
zero-query, zero sample rate — 10 passed.
- Affected neighbours (`ContentSecurityPolicyTest`, `DiscordFunnelTest`,
`AboutPageTest`, `FaqPageTest`, `DbOutageLeavesTest`, allowlist): 48
passed.
- `pint --test` clean; `phpstan` clean on both changed source files.

