Subject: [PATCH 39/48] feat(auth): return members to their page after Discord
 OAuth (#500)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

Deep links into events dumped guests at `/profile` after the Discord
OAuth round trip. `?next=` is now preserved through join and login,
guarded to relative paths only, so members land back on the page they
came from.

## Changes

- New `App\Support\SafeRedirect` guard: only relative paths pass;
absolute URLs, protocol-relative hosts, backslashes, whitespace/control
chars, and non-strings are rejected.
- `JoinController` and `DiscordLoginController` store a guarded `?next=`
in the session on the way out and consume it on the callback. An
explicit `?next=` beats a stale `url.intended`; absent or hostile keeps
the `/profile` landing.
- Guest CTAs forward `?next=`: join-page one-click link, event-page join
pitches, RSVP login links (path captured at mount so Livewire re-renders
never point at `/livewire/update`).

## Testing

- `tests/Unit/SafeRedirectTest.php`: 3 passed, including
`https://evil.test` rejection.
- `tests/Feature/Auth/ReturnToPageTest.php`: 12 passed in CI on
identical slice content (store/consume on both journeys, hostile values
refused at both ends, guest links); not runnable on this box (no
Postgres).
- `tests/Unit/ProductionRouteAllowlistTest.php`: 4 passed post-rebase
(this was the prior red on #494).
- `pint --test` and `phpstan` clean on all touched files.

## Checklist

- [x] No secrets, real `.env`, `vendor/` or `node_modules/` in the diff
- [x] No changes to `app/Http/Resources/EventResource.php`
- [ ] `composer check` fully green — lint + analyse clean locally; full
suite pending CI on this head

Refs: TOG-9254

