## Summary
Server-enforced honeypot field plus minimum-fill-time trap on public
write forms (member profile Livewire save, RSVP JSON PUT/DELETE).
Bot-speed submissions with the decoy filled are swallowed silently — the
exact success shape, no error, no log, no oracle. Normal submissions are
unaffected.

This replays the TOG-9361-approved slice (72f97ea + 9c93e4f, APPROVE on
substance) onto current main as a clean branch, since shared PR #470 is
conflicting and carries no CI for the SHA.

## Changes
- New app/Support/SpamTrap.php: honeypot + 1s time-trap helpers,
fail-closed on zero stamp.
- MemberProfile save(): validate-before-trap, silent-swallow on trap
signals, stale failure/expired banners reset on the trap path (merge-gap
fix vs main TOG-8137 flags).
- RSVP controller + request: silent-swallow writes with decoy filled.
- Hidden decoy input in the profile blade; feature tests in
tests/Feature/Security/SpamTrapTest.php.

## Testing
- SpamTrapTest + MemberProfileTest + FormLabelCoverageTest: 54 passed
(263 assertions).
- tests/Feature/Events + tests/Feature/Security: 247 passed (1070
assertions).
- Pint clean, phpstan clean on the 4 slice app files.

Refs: TOG-8715

