## Summary
`/up` ignored queue health even though `queue:check-depth` already knew
how to see a backlog. A silent queue backlog is silent RSVP delay — no
500, no log line, the Discord mirror just stops catching up — so `/up`
said "up" through the one outage shape members actually feel. This folds
the probe's counting into the deploy health signal: queue depth plus
oldest-job age in the payload, `degraded` (still HTTP 200, never down)
when deep.

## Changes
- New `App\Support\QueueHealth`: single shared counting
(pending/delayed/reserved/total/failed + oldest wait) with WARN_AT=20 /
CRITICAL_AT=100, used by both readers so they never disagree about
"deep".
- New `HealthCheckController` on `GET /up` (funnel, empty middleware
stack): healthy/degraded at 200; `queue.status: unknown` when the driver
is uncountable or the table won't answer.
- `queue:check-depth` refactored onto the shared counting (no behavior
change; existing command tests still pin its thresholds).
- `tests/Feature/QueueHealthEndpointTest.php`: empty→healthy, warn
edge→degraded at 200 with count + age, literal 500-job
acceptance→degraded with count, critical→still degraded, sync
driver→unknown, refused table→200 unknown, funnel middleware pin, app-DB
outage pin.

