## Summary

Pins the invalid-grant probing gap on the agent-events ingress
([TOG-9057](/TOG/issues/TOG-9057) round-5 gap list sec.6): the outer
shield (`throttle:agent-events`, [TOG-8402](/TOG/issues/TOG-8402))
already throttles wrong-credential floods, but no test proved it, and
nothing pinned the no-oracle property.

## Changes

- One Pest test in
`tests/Feature/AgentEvents/AgentEventIngressTest.php`: rapid hits on one
wrong credential 429 with the shared `ThrottleEnvelope` (`429` +
`Retry-After`, no stack); a near-miss and an unrelated guess get
byte-comparable flat 401s (same reason/message/body shape);
per-credential buckets stay isolated; the valid caller still gets 201;
shield-refused hits write no audit rows.

## Testing

- New test: 1 passed (37 assertions) on `two_web_test_tog9250`.
- `AgentEvents` + `Throttling` + `HealthCheck`: 49 passed (357
assertions).
- Full Feature suite: 987 passed, 3 failed — all 3 are
`EventRsvpRosterTest` failing on the sandbox's missing `ext-intl`
(Filament pagination blade), unrelated to this change; intl is a
composer requirement in CI.
- `pint --test`: clean. `phpstan`: 79 errors vs 69 baseline on the
pristine file (Pest DSL noise, same class as pre-existing).

Refs: TOG-9250

