Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Summary

Pre-boot taps on /events and /events/past landed in the unbound window:
the "I'm in" button rendered but `wire:click` was not yet bound, so the
tap did nothing with no announcement. The layout guard disables pre-boot
buttons and answers pre-boot link taps politely until Livewire boots.

## Changes

- `resources/views/components/layouts/app.blade.php`: pre-boot guard on
deferred pages — disables `button[wire:click]`, marks `a[wire:click]`
with `aria-disabled` plus a capture-phase stop-and-announce, lifts both
on `livewire:initialized`; the ready line speaks only if a tap was
actually blocked.
- `tests/Support/DeferredLivewireBoot.php` + `tests/Pest.php`: shared
`waitForLivewireBoot()` (bound runtime AND lifted guard).
- `tests/Feature/Livewire/DeferredPrebootGuardTest.php`: static contract
on both deferred pages, server markup untouched, guard absent on the
non-deferred show page.
- `tests/Browser/EventsRsvpTest.php`, `MobileClickPathTest.php`: boot
waits before every `wire:click` control click; new CDP pre-boot window
test (blocked script → disabled button, no write, recovery boots and
answers).

## Testing

- `php artisan test tests/Feature/Livewire/` — 127 passed (419
assertions) on the feature branch.
- `php -l` clean on all edited Dusk files;
`assertButtonEnabled/Disabled` and `ChromeDevToolsDriver::execute`
signatures verified against vendored Dusk/php-webdriver.
- Dusk (incl. the new pre-boot window test) runs in CI — no local Chrome
in this workspace.

## Checklist

- [x] `composer check` equivalent run for the touched suites (Feature
green; Dusk is CI-gated)
- [x] No secrets, real `.env`, `vendor/` or `node_modules/` in the diff
- [x] No `app/Http/Resources/EventResource.php` change — contract test
untouched

